Version: 1.10.3

Updates:
1. preventScroll stops the jump at its source; the scrollTop = 0 on close means a reopen starts at the top even if you'd
  scrolled through the options before closing.

  Notes on the flipped-above cases:
  - Select moves select_find_rg to the end of the list and sticks it to the bottom — scrollTop = 0 still shows options
  from the top, as asked.
  - Multi-select uses flex-flow: column-reverse when flipped, whose natural resting scroll position is the bottom. The
  explicit reset is doing real work there. If it ever still rests at the bottom in some browser, that's the reversed
  scroll-origin quirk and the follow-up is a second reset on the open transition's transitionend.